  "query_preview": "/Friday through Tuesday/...\nAn upper level trough will remain in place along the Pacific\nNorthwest coast through the period with an upper level ridge\nto the east. The resulting southwest flow will continue to \nusher in a much drier airmass. Shower/storm chances will \ngenerally be less than 20% and confined to the higher terrain \nand along the Idaho/Nevada border. The pattern will bring hot, \ndry, and breezy conditions through the weekend and into early \nnext week. Lower valley highs will remain in the upper 90s to \naround 100 degrees. Winds each day will gust 15-30 mph, \nstrongest in open, elevated areas including the high desert of \nsoutheast Oregon and southwest Idaho south of the Snake River. \nSmoke may impact the area through the period, especially across \nsoutheast Oregon.",
